Package: idmapper
Title: Entity Resolution and Identity Graphs Across Multiple Data Sources
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Gordon", "McDonald", , "gordon.mcdonald@sydney.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Resolve the same real-world entity (for example a person or a
    project) as it appears under different identifiers (email address,
    staff ID, unikey, project shortcode, and so on) across multiple,
    separately maintained data sources. Identifier columns are tagged with
    mark_id(), added to an undirected identity graph with
    add_to_identity_graph() (two identifiers become linked whenever they
    co-occur on the same row of the same dataset), and each connected
    component of that graph is collapsed into a single master identity
    with generate_master_identity_table(). join_master_ids() then attaches
    the resulting master ID back onto any dataset carrying marked
    identifier columns.
